+.. SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+
+===============================================
+PARP per-memcg tier-2 watermarks and prediction
+===============================================
+
+PARP can maintain two headroom watermarks for every non-root memory cgroup.
+The state is not global: each cgroup owns its configuration, EWMA samples,
+arrival estimate, delayed work and counters.  A charge in a nested cgroup
+updates that cgroup and each non-root ancestor independently because memory
+accounting is hierarchical.
+
+Both the global switch and the cgroup switch default to zero.  Therefore this
+facility does not change reclaim until explicitly enabled.
+
+This feature is compiled only when ``CONFIG_PARP_TIER2=y``. The option is in
+the centralized LZX PARP experiment menu and defaults to ``n``.
+
+The MGLRU memcg-bin scorer has a second, independent build switch,
+``CONFIG_PARP_RECLAIM_BIN_SCORE``.  It defaults to ``n`` and depends on
+``CONFIG_PARP_TIER2``.  Even when compiled in, reclaim-bin scoring is active
+only when PARP is in APPLY mode, ``vm.parp_reclaim_bin_enabled`` is one, and
+the target cgroup's ``memory.tier2_enabled`` is one.  The cgroup flag acts as
+the experiment-scope marker; ``vm.tier2_predict_enabled`` may remain zero so
+no Tier2 prediction or proactive reclaim runs in a bin-only ablation.
+Otherwise MGLRU uses its native random bin placement and random starting bin.
+.. lzx-note
+
+For workloads launched as systemd scopes below an enabled experiment slice,
+the scorer uses the nearest enabled ancestor's Tier2 headroom policy while
+retaining the leaf cgroup for application-prior lookup.  This makes a policy
+set on the test slice cover its dynamically created children without silently
+changing unrelated sibling cgroups.  Runtime coverage is exported in
+``/sys/kernel/debug/parp/reclaim_bin_stats``; in particular, non-zero
+``inherited_hits`` and ``scored`` prove that descendant pages used the scorer.
+
+.. lzx-note: reclaim-bin hierarchy contract and auditable coverage counters.
+
+Prediction-cold first-pass pressure
+===================================
+
+``CONFIG_PARP_RECLAIM_COLD_AGGRESSIVE`` adds a third, independent treatment
+on top of reclaim-bin ordering.  It does nothing unless PARP is in APPLY mode,
+``vm.parp_reclaim_bin_enabled=1`` and
+``vm.parp_reclaim_cold_aggressive_enabled=1``.  A leaf memcg must also have a
+fresh application binding and application prediction from ``/dev/myfs``;
+headroom-only fallback scores and unrelated pressure-generator cgroups cannot
+activate this treatment.  .. lzx-note
+
+For prediction bins zero through ``vm.parp_reclaim_cold_bin_max`` (default
+two), the policy temporarily changes only the current memcg's scan control:
+
+* bin zero lowers reclaim priority by three levels and raises swappiness to at
+  least 140;
+* bin one lowers priority by two levels and raises swappiness to at least 120;
+* bin two lowers priority by one level and raises swappiness to at least 100.
+
+Lower priority values scan exponentially more pages, so these settings provide
+approximately 8x, 4x and 2x first-visit scan budgets.  Dirty-page writeback is
+permitted for that visit.  Swappiness stays below anonymous-only mode, allowing
+anonymous, clean file and dirty file pages to participate together.  The
+caller's original priority, writeback permission and swappiness are restored
+before the next memcg is visited; high-probability and unbound cgroups therefore
+retain their native pressure.  Existing swap availability, memcg protection,
+``memory.min``/``memory.low`` and reclaim target termination are not bypassed.
+.. lzx-note
+
+``/sys/kernel/debug/parp/reclaim_cold_stats`` is read-only evidence for
+experiments.  ``passes``, ``scanned``, ``reclaimed``, the per-bin pass counts
+and promotion counters distinguish an enabled switch from an effective action.
+Prediction publication remains exclusively on ``/dev/myfs``.  .. lzx-note
+
+Watermarks and EWMA
+===================
+
+For a cgroup with a finite ``memory.max``::
+
+  headroom = memory.max - memory.current
+  alloc_wmark = max(PAGE_SIZE, memory.max * alloc_scale / 10000)
+  demote_wmark = max(alloc_wmark,
+                     memory.max * demote_scale / 10000)
+
+The defaults are 100 (1 percent) and 300 (3 percent), respectively.  Thus the
+demote watermark is reached first as headroom falls, while the alloc watermark
+is the more urgent level.
+
+Future working-set gate
+=======================
+
+``CONFIG_PARP_TIER2_WSS_PREDICT`` adds an independently switchable gate in
+front of Tier2 reclaim.  The resident service combines each LSTM next-app
+probability with continuously observed GUI and fixture cgroup memory to submit
+three values atomically through ``/dev/myfs`` ABI v2:
+
+``predicted_workingset_bytes``
+  Probability-weighted near-horizon working set for the current foreground
+  application and the likely next applications.
+
+``predicted_resident_bytes``
+  The part of that predicted set still resident in a live application cgroup.
+
+``predicted_growth_bytes``
+  The non-resident/allocation demand, computed as working set minus resident.
+
+The estimate names the exact Tier2 policy cgroup inode.  A domain mismatch,
+age over 10 seconds, expiry, malformed data or confidence below 50 percent
+falls back to the configured demote watermark.  Strengthen and relax require
+the same action from two consecutive prediction generations, preventing one
+bad LSTM result from moving the line.  .. lzx-note
+
+The controller has three effective actions:
+
+``STRENGTHEN``
+  Compute ``projected_headroom = current_headroom - predicted_growth``.  Only
+  if the projected allocation would reach the hard alloc reserve (or the
+  complete predicted working set cannot fit below the normal usage line),
+  lower the *usage* watermark, equivalently raise the headroom demote
+  watermark, and enter bounded reclaim earlier.  The reserve is capped at 10
+  percent of ``memory.max``.  .. lzx-note
+
+``NORMAL``
+  Keep the configured demote watermark and existing EWMA scheduling.
+
+``RELAX``
+  If future demand is already resident and growth fits the hard allocation
+  reserve, and projected headroom remains above the original demote reserve,
+  raise the usage watermark (lower headroom demote to alloc) and skip stale
+  speculative work while headroom remains above the configured demote line.
+  Crossing the original demote watermark overrides relax and restores
+  ``NORMAL`` immediately.  This guard prevents delayed Tier2 work from being
+  transferred into the allocating task as direct reclaim.  .. lzx-note
+
+This gate changes only proactive Tier2 timing.  It neither bypasses normal
+memcg limits nor guarantees that a low-quality LSTM prediction is beneficial;
+the freshness, confidence, hysteresis and hard-line checks are deliberately
+fail-closed to protect fault/refault results.
+
+The EWMA follows the Huawei v4 design::
+
+  ewma = (previous_ewma * 15 + headroom) / 16
+
+When the EWMA is falling, PARP predicts the time to the demote watermark as::
+
+  delta = previous_ewma - ewma
+  predicted_ms = (headroom - demote_wmark) * elapsed_ms / delta
+
+``predicted_ms`` is -1 when headroom is stable/rising, and zero after the
+demote watermark has already been reached.  Samples closer than one
+millisecond are coalesced so that the rate always has a meaningful timebase.
+
+Scheduling
+==========
+
+Prediction work is considered when::
+
+  0 < predicted_ms <= tier2_predict_latency_ms *
+                       tier2_predict_horizon_ratio
+
+It is queued after ``max(1, predicted_ms - tier2_predict_latency_ms)``
+milliseconds.  The earliest outstanding deadline wins, preventing frequent
+charges from continually postponing work.  The work rechecks current
+headroom, rejects a stale estimate after recovery, and starts bounded
+proactive memcg reclaim.  That reclaim uses the normal MGLRU/PARP path.
+
+Each proactive attempt is capped at 1024 pages.  A successful attempt enters
+a 250 ms cooldown; a zero-progress attempt enters a 1000 ms cooldown.  Charge
+hooks cannot re-arm reclaim during that interval.  This is a global bound on
+the repeated work, rather than only a per-call bound, and prevents a cgroup
+that remains below the watermark from spinning in a one-millisecond reclaim
+loop.  ``memory.tier2_stats`` exposes the cooldown, skipped re-arms,
+zero-progress attempts and RELAX-to-NORMAL safety overrides.  .. lzx-note
+
+Global sysctls
+==============
+
+``vm.tier2_predict_enabled``
+  Master switch, 0 or 1.  Default 0. It gates proactive reclaim and PARP's
+  prediction/headroom-based MGLRU memcg-bin ordering, so an OFF versus
+  Tier2-only experiment has one explicit global runtime treatment switch.
+
+``vm.tier2_predict_latency_ms``
+  Expected prediction/reclaim latency, 0 through 1000 ms.  Default 100.
+
+``vm.tier2_predict_horizon_ratio``
+  Scheduling horizon multiplier, 0 through 100.  Default 3.
+
+``vm.parp_reclaim_bin_enabled``
+  Independent MGLRU memcg-bin APPLY switch, 0 or 1.  Default 0.  It requires
+  PARP APPLY mode and an experiment-scope cgroup with
+  ``memory.tier2_enabled=1``, but it does not enable Tier2 proactive reclaim.
+  This permits an exact same-kernel bin OFF/APPLY comparison while the LSTM
+  service and ``/dev/myfs`` prediction stream remain identical.  .. lzx-note
+
+``vm.parp_reclaim_cold_aggressive_enabled``
+  Independent prediction-cold pressure switch, 0 or 1.  It defaults to zero
+  and requires reclaim-bin APPLY.  Use zero for bin-only and one for the
+  bin-plus-pressure ablation.  .. lzx-note
+
+``vm.parp_reclaim_cold_bin_max``
+  Greatest prediction bin allowed to receive increased first-pass pressure,
+  0 through 7.  The default is 2.  .. lzx-note
+
+``vm.tier2_wss_predict_enabled``
+  Runtime working-set gate, 0 or 1.  It exists only with
+  ``CONFIG_PARP_TIER2_WSS_PREDICT=y`` and defaults to 1.  Set it to 0 for an
+  exact same-kernel Tier2-without-WSS ablation; Tier2 then uses its original
+  fixed demote watermark.  .. lzx-note
+
+  The two-generation filter controls entry into ``RELAX`` and ``STRENGTHEN``.
+  ``memory.tier2_stats`` reports that accepted value as
+  ``workingset_policy_action`` and the current live-headroom result as
+  ``workingset_action``.  The live result exits an exceptional action
+  immediately when its condition disappears, so a recovered cgroup does not
+  continue reclaiming until the next user-space event.  .. lzx-note
+
+``vm.tier2_wss_strengthen_enabled``
+  Independent APPLY switch for the WSS ``STRENGTHEN`` action, 0 or 1.  It
+  defaults to 0.  With the switch off, prediction still records an accepted
+  ``STRENGTHEN`` in ``workingset_policy_action`` and its counters, while the
+  effective action is clamped to ``NORMAL`` and cannot raise the proactive
+  reclaim watermark.  Enable it only after the future-cold page selector has
+  demonstrated useful effective-tier or reclaim-bin coverage.  .. lzx-note
+
+Cgroup v2 files
+===============
+
+Each non-root memory cgroup has these files:
+
+``memory.tier2_enabled``
+  Per-cgroup switch, 0 or 1.  Default 0.
+
+``memory.tier2_alloc_scale`` and ``memory.tier2_demote_scale``
+  Per-cgroup ratios in units of 1/10000, range 0 through 10000.
+
+``memory.tier2_alloc_wmark`` and ``memory.tier2_demote_wmark``
+  Current watermarks in bytes.
+
+``memory.tier2_headroom``
+  Current finite-limit headroom in bytes.  Zero is reported for an unlimited
+  cgroup, for which prediction is disabled.
+
+``memory.tier2_below``
+  Current ``alloc`` and ``demote`` threshold states.
+
+``memory.tier2_stats``
+  Configuration, live values, EWMA, predicted time and per-cgroup counters.
+  WSS builds also expose the effective headroom/usage watermark, predicted
+  working set/resident/growth, raw and hysteresis-filtered action, confidence,
+  skips, fallbacks, hard-line overrides and live-action restores.  .. lzx-note
+
+Example
+-------
+
+For ``/sys/fs/cgroup/my-app``::
+
+  echo 1073741824 > /sys/fs/cgroup/my-app/memory.max
+  echo 100 > /sys/fs/cgroup/my-app/memory.tier2_alloc_scale
+  echo 300 > /sys/fs/cgroup/my-app/memory.tier2_demote_scale
+  echo 1 > /sys/fs/cgroup/my-app/memory.tier2_enabled
+  sysctl -w vm.tier2_predict_enabled=1
+  cat /sys/fs/cgroup/my-app/memory.tier2_stats
+
+Configure each application cgroup separately.  Changing one cgroup's scales
+or enabling state does not modify any sibling's watermarks or EWMA history.
+Both the global switch and the target cgroup switch must be one before Tier2
+can score that cgroup or start proactive reclaim.
+
+.. lzx-note: independent build and APPLY-only runtime gating.
